# Laziness proof: filter + head never evaluates the error element.
# Element 1 (value 1) passes the predicate and satisfies head.
# Element 3 ([/ 1 0]) is the laziness sentinel — it would error if forced, but head returns
# before the filter machinery reaches it. Elements beyond the first match are never evaluated.
[filtered: [filter [fn [x] [> x 0]] [1 2 [/ 1 0]]]]
[result: [head filtered]]
===
Dict({"result": Int(1)})
